            text: "Yes. The sealer cures on the pavement, not in the air. Black asphalt in direct sun can run 20 to 40°F hotter than the air, while a shaded driveway on a cool morning can sit well below air temperature. An infrared thermometer pointed at the surface tells you the number that actually counts.",
