            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Enormously. Water-based sealer dries by losing water to the air, and humid air takes it slowly. At 85 per cent humidity a coat that would be dry to touch in 4 hours can take 12, and heavy dew overnight can rewet a film that was not fully cured and leave it blotchy.",
