        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Read 50°F on the pail as 55°F on the pavement, with the first night staying above 50°F and no rain for 24 hours. Measure the surface rather than trusting the air, work in the morning, and in a heatwave mist before you pour.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            A water-based sealer that freezes or chills before it cures is not slow, it is ruined. When the forecast is marginal the cheapest decision you can make is to leave the pail closed and try again next week.
          </p>
        </div>

